        "ru-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "a0c1bc5a-6939-34f7-b404-3f76c0c89622",
                "word": "наутёк",
                "pos": "adv",
                "lang_code": "ru",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "166bd508-68fa-300e-bba9-2c1c9a4ad401",
                        "entry_id": "a0c1bc5a-6939-34f7-b404-3f76c0c89622",
                        "glosses": [
                            "разг., обратиться в бегство, убегая, спасаясь"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "в сочетании с глаголами движения"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "258df59a-e7c0-48a3-8dd9-f94cf0ae23b3",
                                "sense_id": "166bd508-68fa-300e-bba9-2c1c9a4ad401",
                                "text": "Но, едва я сделал шаг в сторону девочки, как львёнок совершенно переменился: он широко раскрыл внезапно позеленевшие глаза, смешно зашипел и, показав острейшие молочные зубки, пустился наутёк."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7844eef1-7659-45e4-b0c5-c2cec2181650",
                        "source_entry_id": "a0c1bc5a-6939-34f7-b404-3f76c0c89622",
                        "source_sense_id": "166bd508-68fa-300e-bba9-2c1c9a4ad401",
                        "source_sense_description": "пуститься, побежать наутёк",
                        "target_lang_word": "take to one's heels",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "take to one's heels",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "502b493e-4436-3319-84eb-e61ab4fda329",
                                        "entry_id": "6181eb50-0166-3809-b6ed-7292b7bdcc7e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To leave, especially to flee or run away."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "idiomatic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a292dea3-1e66-44f0-95a6-1a413ac89384",
                                                "sense_id": "502b493e-4436-3319-84eb-e61ab4fda329",
                                                "text": "[T]hen, confused and frightened, he took to his heels; and, not knowing what he did, made off as fast as he could lay his feet to the ground."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3d0cc42e-3abf-4c3d-bc6a-48b0f6941841",
                                                "sense_id": "502b493e-4436-3319-84eb-e61ab4fda329",
                                                "text": "Of a sudden, however, a man broke from their company, took to his heels, and fled into the church."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "87e3b42c-b1a2-4ed6-89c9-f5362eb6d63b",
                                                "sense_id": "502b493e-4436-3319-84eb-e61ab4fda329",
                                                "text": "After returning the fire three times, Peale's men saw the enemy formed near the college take to their heels."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9c0f498b-cfcf-4d17-991c-e7e90d99b8ba",
                                                "sense_id": "502b493e-4436-3319-84eb-e61ab4fda329",
                                                "text": "Often tax defaulters would take to their heels on sighting the tax collectors."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "024905e2-a063-4718-a7f9-28aa2337ae8f",
                        "source_entry_id": "a0c1bc5a-6939-34f7-b404-3f76c0c89622",
                        "source_sense_id": "166bd508-68fa-300e-bba9-2c1c9a4ad401",
                        "source_sense_description": "пуститься, побежать наутёк",
                        "target_lang_word": "show a clean pair of heels",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "show a clean pair of heels",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b4aaba49-a376-3ac8-b28a-02199bc46e6a",
                                        "entry_id": "acf4e44e-e94e-33da-bca9-41603acc3896",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To run away; to make an escape quickly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "idiomatic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ea6a83c7-8f98-4d24-8eef-52acdd7e7114",
                                                "sense_id": "b4aaba49-a376-3ac8-b28a-02199bc46e6a",
                                                "text": "‘[...]No, gentlemen; he'll always show ’em a clean pair of heels very early in the scuffle, and sneak away.’"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "56193121-3a97-40c2-b61d-1dad77366071",
                                                "sense_id": "b4aaba49-a376-3ac8-b28a-02199bc46e6a",
                                                "text": "But in the second column the \"Britannia\" Pacific , though with one coach less, showed a cleaner pair of heels, [...]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0d672c64-3b8c-450c-abc7-450788220919",
                                                "sense_id": "b4aaba49-a376-3ac8-b28a-02199bc46e6a",
                                                "text": "The two German ships soon showed us and the battle-cruiser Indefatigable in company, a clean pair of heels, though the cruiser HMS Dublin managed to keep them in sight until they disappeared into the Straits of Messina to coal."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7e9d9ebe-1b9a-4d8c-a8f2-bde0fd261b36",
                                                "sense_id": "b4aaba49-a376-3ac8-b28a-02199bc46e6a",
                                                "text": "During the melee the suspect had run off, showing a clear pair of heels."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1f5ea25f-fa60-40f3-8336-9b14d9d9890d",
                        "source_entry_id": "a0c1bc5a-6939-34f7-b404-3f76c0c89622",
                        "source_sense_id": "166bd508-68fa-300e-bba9-2c1c9a4ad401",
